# The same argument presuming the open formula Wings x under the binder:
# since 2026-10-20 a presumption in its context, [?x:Animal] |- Wings ?x
# (tasks.org, aida-discourse-referents); what a counter-instance does to it
# is the follow-up (b)/(d).
lk.
declare Animal : type.
declare Bird, Wings, Flies : Animal -> bool.
declare wf : (forall x:Animal, Wings [x] -> Flies [x]).
argument birds_fly : (forall x:Animal, Bird [x] -> Flies [x]).
elim.
elim b.
cut (forall x:Animal, Wings [x] -> Flies [x]) r.
axiom wf.
elim [x].
elim.
by default.
next.
axiom r.
dixi.
